    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **45 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `checkDigit` field \u2014 a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the `customerCode`.\n\nFollowing the codebase's existing pattern for derived Owner fields (`membershipNumber`, `initials`, `locality`, etc.), which are declared read-only in the OpenAPI schema and auto-mapped from getter methods on the `Owner` model via MapStruct, I made two changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `checkDigit` property (integer, 0\u20139) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains a `checkDigit` field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added `getCheckDigit()`, which computes the standard Luhn check digit over the decimal digits of `customerCode` (ignoring non-digits, right-to-left doubling starting from the rightmost digit), matching the algorithm the test uses exactly. It returns `null` when `customerCode` is unassigned.\n\nMapStruct's `toOwnerDto` picks up the getter automatically, so the field is populated in the API response with no controller or mapper changes needed.\n\nThe new `Cp31Tests` passes and the full suite remains green.",
